      "problem": "Subtract $5{v}^{4}+6{v}^{3}+9$ from $2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "We put a minus sign between the two polynomials, distribute it over the second polynomial, collect like terms, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2)-(5{v}^{4}+6{v}^{3}+9) & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}+{v}^{3}+2-5{v}^{4}-6{v}^{3}-9 & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}+(1-6){v}^{3}+(2-9) & = \\\\ 2{v}^{5}-5{v}^{4}-5{v}^{3}-7 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
